<title>USA: Lincoln National sets $2.61/shr dividend.</title>
<headline>Lincoln National sets $2.61/shr dividend.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WAYNE, Ind. 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lincoln National Convertible Securities Fund Inc said Wednesday its board declared a dividend of $2.61 per share, payable January 14, 1997, record December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>It said the dividend, the highest in its history, is composed of a regular quarterly dividend of $0.24 per share, $2.35 per share in short-term capital gains and an additional distribution of $0.02 per share which represents undistributed net earnings for 1996.</p>
<p>Lincoln National Convertible is a closed-end fund.</p>
<p>		  ((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
